================================================================================

Third-party notices

cryptolite implements no cryptography of its own. Its compat layer
(`src/compat/**`) is a port of crypto-js's framework code (WordArray, modes,
paddings, formats, KDF plumbing); its cryptographic primitives are bundled
from `@noble/hashes` and `@noble/ciphers`; its compat-API TypeScript types are
a port of `@types/crypto-js`. The full license text of each is reproduced
below, as required by its MIT license. (The built `dist/` files also carry
these notices in a banner comment, generated from the same source packages at
build time — see `tsup.config.ts`.)

